From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] postprocess.sh: develop one photo at a time

Each run of dcraw_emu and ImageMagick on a 20MP frame takes hundreds
of megabytes and minutes on this phone. Photos taken in a row were all
developed at once; four pushed 1.6GB into swap and took ten minutes.
Take a lock, so they queue.

---
--- a/data/postprocess.sh	2026-10-15 21:28:55.818320782 +0400
+++ b/data/postprocess.sh	2026-10-15 21:29:17.805768963 +0400
@@ -24,6 +24,12 @@
 	exit 2
 fi
 
+# Develop one photo at a time. Each takes hundreds of megabytes, and photos
+# taken in a row would otherwise all run at once and push the phone into swap.
+if [ -z "$MP_POSTPROCESS_LOCKED" ] && command -v flock > /dev/null; then
+	MP_POSTPROCESS_LOCKED=1 exec flock "${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/tmp}/megapixels-postprocess.lock" "$0" "$@"
+fi
+
 BURST_DIR="$1"
 TARGET_NAME="$2"
 SAVE_DNG="$3"
